## 🚀 Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Python {{python_version}}+
- [uv](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv) (recommended) or pip

### Installation

1. Clone the repository:
   ```bash
   git clone <repository-url>
   cd {{project_name}}
   ```

2. Create and activate a virtual environment:
   ```bash
   # Using uv (recommended)
   uv venv
   source .venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate

   # Or using venv
   python -m venv .venv
   source .venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
   ```

3. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   # Using uv
   uv pip install -e .

   # For development
   uv pip install -e ".[dev]"
   ```

### Usage

{{#if include_cli}}
Run the CLI application:
```bash
{{project_name}} --help
{{project_name}} --name "Python"
```
{{/if}}

Use the library in your code:
```python
from {{project_name}}.main import hello_world

print(hello_world())  # Output: Hello, World!
```

## 🧪 Development

### Running Tests

```bash
# Using uv
uv run pytest

# Or directly
pytest
```

### Code Quality

```bash
# Format code
black src/ tests/

# Lint code
flake8 src/ tests/

# Type checking
mypy src/
```

### Building

```bash
# Build package
python -m build

# Or using uv
uv build
```

## 📋 Available Scripts

- `pytest`: Run tests
- `black`: Format code
- `flake8`: Lint code
- `mypy`: Type check
- `python -m build`: Build package

